		"",
		"A grader checks these names exactly:",
		"- Node name `eventLog`, display name \"Event Log\".",
		"- Credential name `eventLogApi` with one field `apiKey` (a password field). The credential sends the key the way the docs say.",
		"- Operation `event.getAll` (\"Get many events\"). Fields: `since` (string, required), `until` (string, optional), `timeZone` (string, default `UTC`; an IANA time zone name such as `Europe/Berlin`), `includeDeleted` (boolean, default false), `returnAll` (boolean, default false), `limit` (number, default 50; used when `returnAll` is false).",
		"  `since` and `until` are ISO 8601 date-times. A value with an offset or `Z` is used as it is. A value without an offset is a local time in `timeZone`.",
		"  `since` is inclusive and `until` is exclusive. When `until` is empty, send no upper bound.",
		"  Follow the `Link` response header for pagination. Do not fetch pages that you do not need.",
		"  The API also returns deleted events (tombstones). Remove them unless `includeDeleted` is true. `limit` counts the items that the node emits.",
		"  Emit one item per event exactly as the API returns it.",
		"",
		"{{format}}",
		"",
		"Work in the current directory. Dependencies are installed: do not install packages. Do not ask questions.",
		"Stop when the node builds, passes the format checks, and works against the API."
